# Optional — Plausible analytics domain
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=kabafence.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth — dual mode (see preview/REUSE_PORT_v4.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: stub — shared password cookie (ADMIN_PASSWORD).
# Credentials: set AUTH_SECRET → email/password against profiles.role.
# When AUTH_SECRET is unset, ADMIN_PASSWORD stub remains the only path.

# Admin scaffold password (REQUIRED in stub mode to sign in at /admin/login)
# WARNING: cookie stub only — NOT production auth.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-before-sharing

# Optional — enables credentials mode (HMAC-signed sessions + profiles.role).
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
# AUTH_SECRET=

# Optional ops note shown in Settings → Security (documentation only — not a role grant).
# ADMIN_ROLES_DOC=Owner: Alice. Editors TBD after Auth.js.

# Data adapter: memory (default) | postgres
# Memory needs no DATABASE_URL (build/demo safe). Postgres needs migrate + seed.
# KABA_DATA_ADAPTER=memory
# KABA_DATA_ADAPTER=postgres
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://kaba:kaba@127.0.0.1:5432/kaba_fence
#
# Local Postgres (optional):
#   docker compose up -d
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://kaba:kaba@127.0.0.1:5432/kaba_fence npm run db:migrate
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://kaba:kaba@127.0.0.1:5432/kaba_fence npm run db:seed
#
# Vercel production (you supply the cloud URL — do not invent one):
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://…          # Neon/Supabase/RDS/etc (often ?sslmode=require)
#   KABA_DATA_ADAPTER=postgres
#   Then migrate+seed once against that URL (local or CI), redeploy.
#
# Credentials demo owner (after seed, or memory adapter):
#   email:    owner@kabafence.example
#   password: change-me-owner
#   Rotate before production — Settings → Security.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe (optional) — see preview/REUSE_PORT_v5.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without keys: Payments UI shows honest “not connected”; build stays key-free.
# With test keys: admin can open Checkout for an invoice deposit; webhook
# records payment rows (idempotent by Stripe event id). No live charges in
# demo unless you set live keys (do not for demos).
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
#
# Canonical public origin (Checkout success/cancel + metadata). Production:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://kaba-platform.vercel.app
#
# Local webhook (optional):
#   stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook
#
# Dashboard webhook (hosted):
#   https://kaba-platform.vercel.app/api/stripe/webhook
#   Events: checkout.session.completed
#
# Customer pay links: /pay/[token] (no admin cookie). Token is on each invoice
# (memory/seed demo: kf_pay_demo_1001_alicia). Public checkout: POST /api/pay/[token]/checkout
# Launch guide: preview/REUSE_PORT_v18.md


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mail (optional) — see preview/REUSE_PORT_v7.md + v19–v23.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without keys: notifyQuoteCreated / notifyPaymentReceived / notifyInvoicePayLink /
# notifyQuietDigest / notifyVisitReminder / auto pay-link-on-sent are honest no-ops
# (ledger still writes; cron routes return 200 + reason). Admin "Email pay link" returns a clear error
# until configured. Prefer Resend: RESEND_API_KEY + MAIL_FROM.
#
# Auto email pay link when invoice first becomes "sent" (idempotent via
# pay_link_notified_at). Default ON when mail is configured.
# KABA_AUTO_EMAIL_PAY_LINK=true   # force on
# KABA_AUTO_EMAIL_PAY_LINK=false  # disable auto; manual Email pay link still works
#
# Auto visit reminders (day before scheduled_for). Default ON when mail configured.
# Idempotent via quotes.visit_reminder_sent_at. Cron: /api/cron/visit-reminders
# KABA_AUTO_VISIT_REMINDERS=true   # force on
# KABA_AUTO_VISIT_REMINDERS=false  # disable
#
# Quote submit (when configured):
#   1. Owner alert → MAIL_TO_OWNERS (else published site email)
#      + always BCC camoren222@gmail.com (hardcoded QUOTE_OWNER_ALWAYS_COPY)
#   2. Customer confirmation → quote.email (elegant HTML + plain text)
#
# MAIL_FROM="Kaba Fence <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
# MAIL_TO_OWNERS=kabafencellc@gmail.com
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_SECURE=false
#
# Vercel (production):
#   vercel env add MAIL_FROM production --project kaba-platform
#   vercel env add MAIL_TO_OWNERS production --project kaba-platform
#   vercel env add RESEND_API_KEY production --project kaba-platform
# Then redeploy. Verify domain/from in Resend dashboard first.
# Recommended MAIL_TO_OWNERS: kabafencellc@gmail.com
# (camoren222@gmail.com always receives a BCC copy in code — no need to list it,
#  but listing it in MAIL_TO_OWNERS is fine; send dedupes.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cron (Vercel) — gone-quiet digest + visit reminders
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# vercel.json schedules:
#   GET /api/cron/quiet-digest      at 0 12 * * *  UTC (= 07:00 CDT / 06:00 CST)
#   GET /api/cron/visit-reminders   at 15 12 * * * UTC (= 07:15 CDT / 06:15 CST)
#
# CRON_SECRET — random ≥16 chars. Vercel sends Authorization: Bearer <value>
# on cron invocations. Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=
#
# Vercel production:
#   vercel env add CRON_SECRET production --project kaba-platform
#   # also ensure MAIL_FROM + RESEND_API_KEY (+ MAIL_TO_OWNERS) are set
#   vercel --prod --yes --project kaba-platform
#
# Manual test (after deploy or locally with CRON_SECRET in .env.local):
#   curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" \
#     https://kaba-platform.vercel.app/api/cron/quiet-digest
#   curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" \
#     https://kaba-platform.vercel.app/api/cron/visit-reminders
#
# Without mail keys the routes return 200 + reason (honest no-op).
# Quiet digest recipients: MAIL_TO_OWNERS + always BCC camoren222@gmail.com.
# Visit reminders: To customer; BCC MAIL_TO_OWNERS + camoren222@gmail.com.
# See preview/REUSE_PORT_v21.md (digest) and v23.md (visit reminders).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public chat — Vercel AI Gateway (GPT-4o mini) — see preview/REUSE_PORT_v28.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without credentials: /api/chat returns the existing rules-engine replies
# (honest fallback; ChatWidget still works). No secrets are invented here.
#
# Model (hardcoded in src/lib/chat/gateway.ts): openai/gpt-4o-mini
#
# Local development — create a key at:
#   https://vercel.com/dashboard → AI Gateway → API Keys
# Then set:
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
#
# Or pull a short-lived OIDC token (expires ~12h):
#   vercel link   # project: kaba-platform
#   vercel env pull .env.local
#   # uses VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN; prefer `vercel dev` so it refreshes
#
# Vercel production / preview (kaba-platform ONLY):
#   Prefer OIDC — no AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY required on the deployment.
#   Optional: still add AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY if you want a static key.
#   Do NOT invent or paste a key into this repo. User adds it in the dashboard:
#     vercel env add AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY production --project kaba-platform
#   Then redeploy. Confirm AI Gateway is enabled for the team / project.
#
# Cost note: GPT-4o mini via AI Gateway is billed at provider token rates
# (Gateway adds no markup). Keep maxOutputTokens low (chat route caps ~450).
# Set a team/project budget in the Vercel AI Gateway dashboard.
